<ServiceLayout title="UX Strategy & Product Design Services" description="UX audits, product design, interactive prototypes and design systems with Angelo Manzano Jr. Based in Palm Bay, Florida; working with teams nationwide." label="ChrowmDesigns / Services" heading="Design support, from the question to the interface." intro="I’m Angelo Manzano Jr., an independent UX strategist and product designer. I help agencies and in-house teams work through complex digital experiences, decide what matters, and bring the design into focus.">
  <section class="service-section" aria-labelledby="services-heading">
    <h2 id="services-heading">Where I can help</h2>
    <div class="service-grid">
      <div><h3>UX strategy & audits</h3><p>When a website or product is difficult to navigate, start with the experience behind the screen. I examine user journeys, information architecture, and interface decisions to identify friction and define the next steps.</p><p>Depending on the brief, the work can include a UX review, journey mapping, a revised content structure, and a prioritized set of design recommendations.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Website & digital product design</h3><p>For a new experience or a redesign, I turn requirements into user flows, wireframes, and detailed interfaces. The work considers desktop and mobile together, with attention to content, navigation, and interaction.</p><p>Deliverables can include page layouts, interface states, responsive designs, and design notes for implementation.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Interactive prototypes</h3><p>A prototype gives your team something concrete to discuss before development. I connect key screens and interactions so stakeholders can walk through the experience and make decisions with context.</p><p>We agree on the journeys and level of detail first, whether the goal is exploring an idea or reviewing an established direction.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Design systems & UI consistency</h3><p>As a product grows, inconsistencies make both design and implementation harder. I help organize reusable components, interface patterns, and visual rules around the needs of the product.</p><p>The scope can range from a focused component library to guidance for extending an existing system.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="service-section" aria-labelledby="relevant-work"><h2 id="relevant-work">See the thinking in practice</h2><div class="service-grid">
